    "morphology": "Fronto-central negativity around 200 to 350 ms (measured here at FCz). A family of subcomponents (N2a/MMN, N2b, N2c, and the posterior N2pc).",
    "meaning": "Linked to cognitive control: conflict monitoring, response inhibition, and the detection of novelty or mismatch. The posterior N2pc indexes the spatial selection of a target.",
    "task": "Go/NoGo, flanker and Stroop conflict tasks, visual search (N2pc), and oddball paradigms."
